window.products.push({"id":896459,"name":"Cheap Ceiling Tiles #204 Antique Silver 2x2 Fire Rated Can Be Glue on Any Flat Surface.suspended Ceiling!glue On,nail On,staple On,tape On!affordable,","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61pvInJED7L._AC_.jpg","description":"Ceiling Tile Material is Rigid PVC, Poly Vinyl Chloride, standard 24 inch x 24 inch x 0.50 mm. Ceiling Tiles is UL Class A Fire Rated. Ceiling Tile is easy to cut with regular scissors for installation as drop in grid suspended or glue up with overlapping edges. If desired Ceiling Tile can be painted with any good quality paint and is washable using water and mild detergent. Always plan, measure twice, cut once and test before starting your project. Installation Instructions Glue Up Overlapping Edges. 1.Glue up Installation with overlapping edges, approximately one-quarter inch overlapping edge, the surface must be smooth, clean, free of dirt, dust or oil & follow manufacturer’s instructions 2.Prepare the surface wipe off the ceiling surface and make it smooth and even. Remove loose plaster, paint, wall paper etc. 3.Determine starting point of glue up process use a tape measure and chalk line find center of room width and length, the first tile to glue up should be in one of the four quadrants or at 90-degree angle. 4.The glue we recommend is Loctite All Purpose Construction Adhesive, Contact Cement Gel or Contact Cement. 5.Apply the adhesive to a smooth clean dry surface. 6.Place the first ceiling tile sheet in the required position, first sheet at the 90 degree point, and press firmly. 7.Be careful with adhesive not to get on hands or on front face of ceiling tile and have moist sponge or follow manufactures recommendation for cleanup and removal of any excess or adhesive spillage. 8.Continue the process until completion. You now have a beautiful ceiling. Installation Grid Suspended Ceiling System. 1.Installation in Grid Suspended Ceiling System, standard 2 ft x 2 ft size, we recommend simply insert PVC Ceiling Tile beneath existing acoustical ceiling tile. 2.We recommend painting the T-Bar or Grids with spray paint to match or coordinate to match your preferences. 3.Continue the process until completion. You now have a beautiful ceiling.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61pvInJED7L._AC_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"CTBU","source_asin":"B00319P85E","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-896459","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00319P85E","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B00319P85E","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
